[a] Get the Depth Buffer and Depth Texture Mip Chain (max-4 for each higher level)

[b] Do Culling in the Geometry Shader

=========
[a] Use previous Frame's depth buffer reprojected 
    OR
    Use the major occluders to generate the Depth Buffer at Full resolution

    Then do subsequent full screen quad passes to generate the depth mipchain


[b] Culling is where there are 2 possible solutions:

   [1]  Hierarchical Rasterization
http://rastergrid.com/blog/2010/10/hierarchical-z-map-based-occlusion-culling/
   	In the Geometry Shader, generate a Bounding Box, Rasterize it based on distance (to decide resolution)
	Compare Bounding Box's min depth with Depth MipChain lower's MAX depth (out of 4 texels)

	If you can trivially reject it, put this information in the Stream Out (Transform Feedback) buffer and move on

	This is your Visibility Stream!!

   [ii] Full Rasterization + Visibility Buffer
https://github.com/nvpro-samples/gl_occlusion_culling
   	Generate the Bounding box and 3 Faces and let it move down the Pipe 

	In the Fragment shader, set a bit in the Visibility Buffer

	
-----

The Visibility Buffer is then consumed by a Compute Shader to generate indices for your MDI call.


